# PTT (Phan-Thien–Tanner) 3D planar-Poiseuille coupled canary for the
# KRK-VE-3D dispatch. The production driver (run_viscoelastic_fvfd_poiseuille_3d)
# drives a periodic x/z, no-slip half-way bounce-back y-wall channel with a
# D3Q19 solvent at nu_s and a polymer feedback F_poly = ∇·τ_p. The conformation
# state is advanced in symmetric log form ψ = log(C). The PTT closure multiplies
# the relaxation by a scalar trace multiplier Y(trC) = 1 + epsilon·(trC − 3)
# (linear variant), enhancing relaxation of stretched modes — producing
# shear-thinning and a bounded steady response (reduced polymer stress / N1
# relative to Oldroyd-B at the same Wi). At epsilon → 0 the result recovers
# Oldroyd-B bit-identically. The variant is numeric: 0 = linear (default),
# 1 = exponential (Y = exp(epsilon·(trC − 3))).
#
# beta = nu_s/(nu_s+nu_p) = 0.5, nu_total = 0.1, lambda = 10, Fx = 1e-5.
Simulation poiseuille_ptt D3Q19

Define Fx = 1e-5

Domain L = 6 x 32 x 6  N = 6 x 32 x 6
Physics Fx = Fx
Rheology ptt { nu_s = 0.05 nu_p = 0.05 lambda = 10 epsilon = 0.2 variant = 0 }
Module viscoelastic

Run 4000 steps
